[{:db/id "q-138881/selection/831fe7c29ca3822fb03cd85bd3480aab21358c3e02bf9226b60fc5cedcc2503f" :answer/id #uuid "891e5c26-c31f-5283-843d-844e46211a7a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2{sec}^{2}⁡t-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-138881/selection/02eef9361a40d7e4c00225f17e455adb93396b7a4d6fef9b95914531f9c3dca3" :answer/id #uuid "964c0021-ca44-5b1a-a9fc-0ee132e37e29" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\operatorname{sec}⁡t+4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-138881/selection/27e35080d26bb343c270131a207f54e0ea681637f4be8fd5a9606d01ab8b913f" :answer/id #uuid "2ea27fb8-06a3-5a06-87b6-d86b8ba2e9c7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4\\operatorname{sec}⁡t+2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-138881/selection/33254f692e5758a82457844e38bed19af424f6b1e3deb961e1c699d195ce2dae" :answer/id #uuid "0c8fcff5-aa5e-5c06-bcf5-6bccd067a1ca" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2{sec}^{2}⁡t+4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-138881/selection/a48812a307b219a3f6ce681ec9cad6c3c64eb88c13966fd1085bca2e7f9b8966" :answer/id #uuid "d02dea46-58e7-55f5-9bcb-1fcb7cbecfa1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{sec}^{2}⁡t-4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-138881/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "f6b4bad3-27ac-5d5a-8326-972f4ea6f1ec" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-138881/selection/33254f692e5758a82457844e38bed19af424f6b1e3deb961e1c699d195ce2dae" :answer-field/choices ["q-138881/selection/831fe7c29ca3822fb03cd85bd3480aab21358c3e02bf9226b60fc5cedcc2503f" "q-138881/selection/02eef9361a40d7e4c00225f17e455adb93396b7a4d6fef9b95914531f9c3dca3" "q-138881/selection/27e35080d26bb343c270131a207f54e0ea681637f4be8fd5a9606d01ab8b913f" "q-138881/selection/33254f692e5758a82457844e38bed19af424f6b1e3deb961e1c699d195ce2dae" "q-138881/selection/a48812a307b219a3f6ce681ec9cad6c3c64eb88c13966fd1085bca2e7f9b8966"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-138881" :question/id #uuid "9ec922f7-fb5c-5c96-9d82-3da583b98300" :question/math-academy-id "q-138881" :question/problem "A body of mass $2\\,\\text{kg}$ is moving in a straight line along the $x$-axis under the action of a single force $F,$ measured in Newtons.\nAt time $t$ seconds, the velocity of the body is given by $v(t)=\\operatorname{tan}⁡t+2t$ meters per second.\nFind an expression for the force acting on the body at time $t.$" :question/worked-solution "According to Newton’s second law\n\n$$\nF=ma,\n$$\n\n \nwhere $F$ is the force, $m$ is the mass, and $a$ is the acceleration.\n\nTo find the acceleration $a(t),$ we differentiate the velocity $v(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{tan}⁡t+2t) \\\\  & ={sec}^{2}⁡t+2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the force, in Newtons, is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F & =ma \\\\  & =2\\cdot ({sec}^{2}⁡t+2) \\\\  & =2{sec}^{2}⁡t+4.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-138881/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d7223f4c-b6aa-5e20-8f6b-1f333bac0da6"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-138881"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-345208/field-1/bc331a42ec531f22b7a405f16ed81c386c405d497af33d95b2ea16340689eb9a" :answer/id #uuid "a47e2ea1-5911-5af6-8d9f-388fcde92ccb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-54e^{2t}\\sin(e^{2t})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-345208/field-1/3f9ba047dcda7e4450827592d452c92747893a11a350ddbb91275c5b5cea5bf7" :answer/id #uuid "890ad7ab-f832-5bbd-8703-1bda9d215d3e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "54e^{2t}\\sin(e^{2t})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-345208/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "db0a69ad-8878-5464-b311-545bda2e2b35" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-345208/field-1/bc331a42ec531f22b7a405f16ed81c386c405d497af33d95b2ea16340689eb9a" :answer-field/choices ["q-345208/field-1/bc331a42ec531f22b7a405f16ed81c386c405d497af33d95b2ea16340689eb9a" "q-345208/field-1/3f9ba047dcda7e4450827592d452c92747893a11a350ddbb91275c5b5cea5bf7"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-345208" :question/id #uuid "a37e0cd1-3596-5af2-9194-435d5855f8a8" :question/math-academy-id "q-345208" :question/problem "A body of mass $9\\,\\text{kg}$ moves along the $x$-axis under the action of a single force $F,$ measured in Newtons.  At time $t$ seconds, the velocity of the body is given by $v(t)=3\\operatorname{cos}⁡({e}^{2t})$ meters per second.  Find an expression for the force acting on the particle at time $t.$\n\n$F(t)=$\n\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "By Newton’s second law,\n\n$$\nF(t)=ma(t),\n$$\n\nwhere $F(t)$ is the force, $m$ is the mass, and $a(t)$ is the acceleration.\n\nTo find the acceleration $a(t),$ we differentiate the velocity $v(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[3\\operatorname{cos}⁡({e}^{2t})] \\\\  & =-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡({e}^{2t})\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{2t}) \\\\  & =-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡({e}^{2t})\\cdot 2{e}^{2t} \\\\  & =-6{e}^{2t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡({e}^{2t}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the force, in Newtons, is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(t) & =ma(t) \\\\  & =9\\cdot [-6{e}^{2t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡({e}^{2t})] \\\\  & =-54{e}^{2t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡({e}^{2t}).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-345208/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d7223f4c-b6aa-5e20-8f6b-1f333bac0da6"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-345208"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-345223/field-1/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "5364993f-c959-5f87-8f90-e78a76d66821" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-345223/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "e7afd2ea-b5c1-5328-8032-7541938d6408" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-345223/field-1/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer-field/choices ["q-345223/field-1/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-345223" :question/id #uuid "05a4a7a9-8c35-544f-a2e7-da58644256f8" :question/math-academy-id "q-345223" :question/problem "A body of mass $\\sqrt{2}\\,\\text{kg}$ is moving in a straight line along the $x$-axis under the action of a single force $F,$ measured in Newtons $(\\text{N}).$  At time $t$ seconds, the velocity of the body is given by $v(t)=\\operatorname{sec}⁡t$ meters per second. \n\nCalculate the magnitude of the force at time $t=\\frac{\\pi }{4}$ seconds. Do not round the answer.\n\nThe magnitude of the force equals\n{{field-1}} $\\text{N}.$" :question/worked-solution "According to Newton’s second law,\n\n$$\nF(t)=ma(t),\n$$\n\nwhere $F(t)$ is the force, $m$ is the mass, and $a(t)$ is the acceleration.\n\nTo find the acceleration $a(t),$ we differentiate the velocity $v(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sec}⁡t) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sec}⁡t\\operatorname{tan}⁡t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs a result, the acceleration at $t=\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\,\\text{s}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(\\frac{\\pi }{4}) & =\\operatorname{sec}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4}) \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the force, in Newtons, is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(\\frac{\\pi }{4}) & =ma(\\frac{\\pi }{4}) \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}\\cdot \\sqrt{2} \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the magnitude of the force is\n\n$$\n|F(\\frac{\\pi }{4})|=|2|=2\\,\\text{N}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-345223/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d7223f4c-b6aa-5e20-8f6b-1f333bac0da6"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-345223"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-138882/selection/f017fe1ff73416171aff8b158c691401001dbcb027f3694a0fc15ed3409e0620" :answer/id #uuid "f6e3f5e6-9cb8-5c0b-83d2-23556169f0c6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3{t}^{2}-2t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-138882/selection/b52ab685fc74444c3846dbe4766080e810d3d9d52aa69d258cbf368a9cb9c5fa" :answer/id #uuid "5135abd7-75f8-59a0-8140-66557a2b50f0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "12{t}^{2}+4t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-138882/selection/c3e4472232907367365f1bcd314b51fdebdffb8e7f307a25f9ab2c768ac51144" :answer/id #uuid "08792690-b840-53f0-b1e1-98ba41d33b9a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "18{t}^{2}-12t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-138882/selection/d6a118165107a1fb14b236ee58a547fd6f2ebca60e187553728318862265e37f" :answer/id #uuid "2dd3b807-c3a0-5055-9b19-42c98da1708b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "18t+12" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-138882/selection/296d9f62bad0208a1d82d863d247f8601e590e6d330eae6f16d17ab2f077cf3f" :answer/id #uuid "bf72cbd3-dd94-540a-8362-f3cf1c112f3e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "9t-6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-138882/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "eb889bcc-ca8e-5a05-8908-d31a5d343660" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-138882/selection/c3e4472232907367365f1bcd314b51fdebdffb8e7f307a25f9ab2c768ac51144" :answer-field/choices ["q-138882/selection/f017fe1ff73416171aff8b158c691401001dbcb027f3694a0fc15ed3409e0620" "q-138882/selection/b52ab685fc74444c3846dbe4766080e810d3d9d52aa69d258cbf368a9cb9c5fa" "q-138882/selection/c3e4472232907367365f1bcd314b51fdebdffb8e7f307a25f9ab2c768ac51144" "q-138882/selection/d6a118165107a1fb14b236ee58a547fd6f2ebca60e187553728318862265e37f" "q-138882/selection/296d9f62bad0208a1d82d863d247f8601e590e6d330eae6f16d17ab2f077cf3f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-138882" :question/id #uuid "253cf769-d1eb-5f48-a820-f2091a94ee95" :question/math-academy-id "q-138882" :question/problem "A body of mass $6\\,\\text{kg}$ is moving in a straight line along the $x$-axis under the action of a single force $F,$ measured in Newtons.\nAt time $t$ seconds, the velocity of the body is given by $v(t)={t}^{3}-{t}^{2}$ meters per second.\nFind an expression for the force acting on the body at time $t.$" :question/worked-solution "According to Newton’s second law\n\n$$\nF=ma,\n$$\n\n \nwhere $F$ is the force, $m$ is the mass, and $a$ is the acceleration.\n\nTo find the acceleration $a(t),$ we differentiate the velocity $v(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{3}-{t}^{2}) \\\\  & =3{t}^{2}-2t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the force, in Newtons, is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F & =ma \\\\  & =6\\cdot (3{t}^{2}-2t) \\\\  & =18{t}^{2}-12t.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-138882/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d7223f4c-b6aa-5e20-8f6b-1f333bac0da6"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-138882"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-345209/field-1/3940a204e403a212ec11d5df7b82c76c39901dfcbc993c755df7e712738f39ed" :answer/id #uuid "4d6c7ee3-056f-5006-add8-ea0b96bbf603" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{(t+1)^2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-345209/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "e0865b0c-fea1-57a3-8ada-e53ed090fe9c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-345209/field-1/3940a204e403a212ec11d5df7b82c76c39901dfcbc993c755df7e712738f39ed" :answer-field/choices ["q-345209/field-1/3940a204e403a212ec11d5df7b82c76c39901dfcbc993c755df7e712738f39ed"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-345209" :question/id #uuid "dc008106-3de7-5b76-a831-099686c669f0" :question/math-academy-id "q-345209" :question/problem "A body of mass $\\frac{1}{2}\\,\\text{kg}$ moves along the $x$-axis under the action of a single force $F,$ measured in Newtons.  At time $t$ seconds, the velocity of the body is given by $v(t)=\\frac{2t}{t+1}$ meters per second.  Find an expression for the force acting on the particle at time $t.$\n\n$F(t)=$\n\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "By Newton’s second law,\n\n$$\nF(t)=ma(t),\n$$\n\nwhere $F(t)$ is the force, $m$ is the mass, and $a(t)$ is the acceleration.\n\nTo find the acceleration $a(t),$ we differentiate the velocity $v(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{2t}{t+1}) \\\\  & =\\frac{(t+1)\\cdot (2t)^{′}-2t\\cdot (t+1)^{′}}{(t+1)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2(t+1)-2t(1)}{(t+1)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(2t+2)-2t}{(t+1)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{(t+1)^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the force, in Newtons, is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(t) & =ma(t) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\frac{2}{(t+1)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{(t+1)^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-345209/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d7223f4c-b6aa-5e20-8f6b-1f333bac0da6"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-345209"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-138907/selection/2f20011da86648ab8b13dddcbc04af24b6385ed5c82707da208dd0115bd17650" :answer/id #uuid "7d6e1ddd-0962-5517-9e06-0e4129354d85" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5\\,\\text{N}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-138907/selection/e2b6ca66ef3c24c96860c4932fc83c1e831de4969088b833835b2483f300ba1c" :answer/id #uuid "6e5b0f1b-2365-53cf-b810-4df5c1706eaa" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8\\,\\text{N}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-138907/selection/ccdd5e5f4add679facfc70b77a019fe77a479ec1fbe982b2a1bfe988fa2119f0" :answer/id #uuid "221bca98-3ad1-5099-b91b-8ffc8f862466" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "20\\,\\text{N}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-138907/selection/e42f276e092b7cab322e1ec7fa913530a697d425b65b926f00dd721e785e646c" :answer/id #uuid "b90355dd-9a3c-594a-a991-71b9b460256e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "12\\,\\text{N}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-138907/selection/f4421e85fc4d73dc5dc0f54e2cc417b8c4f331ae034096fa090ea0bb635d7eef" :answer/id #uuid "23547460-662f-5353-83d9-f56dd1cf691e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "10\\,\\text{N}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-138907/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "377ca35b-447c-5135-bbfa-3af2c5c3c412" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-138907/selection/ccdd5e5f4add679facfc70b77a019fe77a479ec1fbe982b2a1bfe988fa2119f0" :answer-field/choices ["q-138907/selection/2f20011da86648ab8b13dddcbc04af24b6385ed5c82707da208dd0115bd17650" "q-138907/selection/e2b6ca66ef3c24c96860c4932fc83c1e831de4969088b833835b2483f300ba1c" "q-138907/selection/ccdd5e5f4add679facfc70b77a019fe77a479ec1fbe982b2a1bfe988fa2119f0" "q-138907/selection/e42f276e092b7cab322e1ec7fa913530a697d425b65b926f00dd721e785e646c" "q-138907/selection/f4421e85fc4d73dc5dc0f54e2cc417b8c4f331ae034096fa090ea0bb635d7eef"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-138907" :question/id #uuid "aff0d900-0d16-5502-bd82-5d0e6f780ecd" :question/math-academy-id "q-138907" :question/problem "A body of mass $4\\,\\text{kg}$ is moving in a straight line along the $x$-axis under the action of a single force $F,$ measured in Newtons $(\\text{N}).$\nAt time $t$ seconds, the position of the body is given by $s(t)=2{t}^{2}+{e}^{5-t}$ meters.\nCalculate the magnitude of the force at time $t=5$ seconds." :question/worked-solution "According to Newton’s second law\n\n$$\nF=ma,\n$$\n\n \nwhere $F$ is the force, $m$ is the mass, and $a$ is the acceleration.\n\nTo find the velocity $v(t),$ we differentiate the displacement $s(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}s}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2{t}^{2}+{e}^{5-t}) \\\\  & =4t-{e}^{5-t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the acceleration $a(t),$ we differentiate the velocity $v(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4t-{e}^{5-t}) \\\\  & =4-(-{e}^{5-t}) \\\\  & =4+{e}^{5-t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs a result, the acceleration at $t=5\\,\\text{s}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a & =4+{e}^{5-5} \\\\  & =4+1 \\\\  & =5\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the force in Newtons is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F & =ma \\\\  & =4\\cdot (5) \\\\  & =20.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the magnitude of the force is\n\n$$\n|F|=|20|=20\\,\\text{N}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-138907/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e955e35e-c45f-53b9-9f95-332d3e9c648f"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-138907"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-138901/selection/11d699e86833ed28cc2522a932d8d05c81f6efb29dec0e5ed36c8cd907c9fe4e" :answer/id #uuid "878beeac-d61b-5bf0-9a2b-6b41aff66d82" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "24{e}^{2t}-12t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-138901/selection/8d289364e502bed37cb925020785ace28631100f129bb069734ee2ca5c90b6dd" :answer/id #uuid "78658f23-26dd-5b83-a1bc-29519a54624a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "18{e}^{2t}-12t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-138901/selection/49b6ef7718e4a34d0f4b2afd51766289fed0637f8a3a4356ca51f1d40913ebd8" :answer/id #uuid "184eaca3-31bb-5561-8cf6-c0f17fcc7727" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "12{e}^{2t}-18t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-138901/selection/8279c2a869042d7272fca2f36e17ff3f27f433afb4732503ac177ef6b6cfd7db" :answer/id #uuid "ccbbd2ae-3131-53d6-a6ef-b221f80640ea" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "12{e}^{2t}-6t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-138901/selection/2305601e3259d6a97d385aa3998200159005e9a0f6b665fc4de5f3f8dc3e8bda" :answer/id #uuid "4c5325b3-7241-537f-a326-f60477e4a478" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4{e}^{2t}-6t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-138901/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "6e3b8fc4-2210-5501-96fa-fe95a42ffe3b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-138901/selection/49b6ef7718e4a34d0f4b2afd51766289fed0637f8a3a4356ca51f1d40913ebd8" :answer-field/choices ["q-138901/selection/11d699e86833ed28cc2522a932d8d05c81f6efb29dec0e5ed36c8cd907c9fe4e" "q-138901/selection/8d289364e502bed37cb925020785ace28631100f129bb069734ee2ca5c90b6dd" "q-138901/selection/49b6ef7718e4a34d0f4b2afd51766289fed0637f8a3a4356ca51f1d40913ebd8" "q-138901/selection/8279c2a869042d7272fca2f36e17ff3f27f433afb4732503ac177ef6b6cfd7db" "q-138901/selection/2305601e3259d6a97d385aa3998200159005e9a0f6b665fc4de5f3f8dc3e8bda"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-138901" :question/id #uuid "ce8fb41e-d014-5085-a244-2a0981843cf2" :question/math-academy-id "q-138901" :question/problem "A body of mass $3\\,\\text{kg}$ is moving in a straight line along the $x$-axis under the action of a single force $F,$ measured in Newtons.\nAt time $t$ seconds, the position of the body is given by $s(t)={e}^{2t}-{t}^{3}$ meters.\nFind the expression for the force acting on the body at time $t.$" :question/worked-solution "According to Newton’s second law\n\n$$\nF=ma,\n$$\n\n \nwhere $F$ is the force, $m$ is the mass, and $a$ is the acceleration.\n\nTo find the velocity $v(t),$ we differentiate the displacement $s(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}s}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{2t}-{t}^{3}) \\\\  & =2{e}^{2t}-3{t}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the acceleration $a(t),$ we differentiate the velocity $v(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2{e}^{2t}-3{t}^{2}) \\\\  & =4{e}^{2t}-6t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the force in Newtons is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F & =ma \\\\  & =3\\cdot (4{e}^{2t}-6t) \\\\  & =12{e}^{2t}-18t.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-138901/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e955e35e-c45f-53b9-9f95-332d3e9c648f"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-138901"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-345345/field-1/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "5930bfc1-b505-5eb2-8747-afba73ba7203" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-345345/field-1/7845f5bf94d2cfe99f73682a34529955af46f8f5d6f59bb198a07cbc245060af" :answer/id #uuid "1ce59985-a7f4-5f73-a23f-fdccae5d9d9a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-345345/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "1869c403-75e3-5b0f-82a1-cdcc46c7da89" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-345345/field-1/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer-field/choices ["q-345345/field-1/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" "q-345345/field-1/7845f5bf94d2cfe99f73682a34529955af46f8f5d6f59bb198a07cbc245060af"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-345345" :question/id #uuid "e253f00d-234d-5211-a4f0-8165426a2570" :question/math-academy-id "q-345345" :question/problem "A body of mass $\\frac{1}{4}\\,\\text{kg}$ is moving in a straight line along the $x$-axis under the action of a single force $F,$ measured in Newtons $(\\text{N}).$  At time $t>0$ seconds, the position of the body is given by $s(t)={e}^{2t}$ meters.\n\nCalculate the magnitude of the force at time $t=\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\sqrt{2}$ seconds. Do not round the answer.\n\nThe magnitude of the force equals\n{{field-1}} $\\text{N}.$" :question/worked-solution "According to Newton’s second law,\n\n$$\nF(t)=ma(t),\n$$\n\n \nwhere $F(t)$ is the force, $m$ is the mass, and $a(t)$ is the acceleration.\n\nTo find the velocity $v(t),$ we differentiate the displacement $s(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}s}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{2t}) \\\\  & =2{e}^{2t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the acceleration $a(t),$ we differentiate the velocity $v(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2{e}^{2t}) \\\\  & =2\\cdot 2{e}^{2t} \\\\  & =4{e}^{2t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs a result, the acceleration at $t=\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\sqrt{2}\\,\\text{s}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\sqrt{2}) & =4{e}^{2\\cdot \\operatorname{ln}⁡\\sqrt{2}} \\\\  & =4{e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡[{(\\sqrt{2})}^{2}]} \\\\  & =4{e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2} \\\\  & =4\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the force in Newtons is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\sqrt{2}) & =ma(\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\sqrt{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot 8 \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the magnitude of the force is\n\n$$\n|F(2)|=|2|=2\\,\\text{N}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-345345/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e955e35e-c45f-53b9-9f95-332d3e9c648f"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-345345"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-345339/field-1/239238708c0d1770242fc9ae66be7bcd19348e832b5b2596086da47d7ab5a666" :answer/id #uuid "42e48301-3781-5b1f-ac80-f45f4f63437f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\cos(t)-t\\sin(t)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-345339/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "f5b299de-f350-54a7-bf19-2252c4ffc75d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-345339/field-1/239238708c0d1770242fc9ae66be7bcd19348e832b5b2596086da47d7ab5a666" :answer-field/choices ["q-345339/field-1/239238708c0d1770242fc9ae66be7bcd19348e832b5b2596086da47d7ab5a666"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-345339" :question/id #uuid "485f113e-1072-57f0-bd8c-02699b28f536" :question/math-academy-id "q-345339" :question/problem "A body of mass $1\\,\\text{kg}$ is moving in a straight line along the $x$-axis under the action of a single force $F,$ measured in Newtons.  At time $t$ seconds, the position of the particle is given by $s(t)=t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t$ meters.  Find the expression for the force acting on the particle at time $t.$\n\n$F(t)=$\n\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "By Newton’s second law,\n\n$$\nF(t)=ma(t),\n$$\n\nwhere $F(t)$ is the force, $m$ is the mass, and $a(t)$ is the acceleration.\n\nTo find the velocity $v(t),$ we differentiate the displacement $s(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}s}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡t+t\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t) \\\\  & =1\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡t+t\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the acceleration $a(t),$ we differentiate the velocity $v(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡t+t\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+1\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡t+t\\cdot (-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the force, in Newtons, is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(t) & =ma(t) \\\\  & =1\\cdot (2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t) \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-345339/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e955e35e-c45f-53b9-9f95-332d3e9c648f"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-345339"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-138902/selection/dceb8599843d2455753fd3b610098e24c507c3f8042510eb7de7551e8d895488" :answer/id #uuid "c093a4cd-6154-558b-880b-dec91848686a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5}{t\\sqrt{t}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-138902/selection/53e8c89f42976ed9e127d262e2f084ed51bc514efc5689e86b89aef2712cf66d" :answer/id #uuid "88bf2c30-aa47-50f0-84cc-06d8c4f1c600" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5t\\sqrt{t}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-138902/selection/2bd062a58e73398ad0d40efa61e4ff7757c19b4ffa3bc28d310e025ccf1dab75" :answer/id #uuid "f2bf88e1-b72c-5cd8-95ad-7210fbda20b3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1+\\frac{5}{t\\sqrt{t}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-138902/selection/d8b0559a2ad692afd9d39c5b69c4476f36bad80b246506190982af18acbb4d61" :answer/id #uuid "5ba95a31-b049-5f75-95cd-b309a553ef34" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{t\\sqrt{t}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-138902/selection/7340d7cc3561e241b79868dd2293b7678cb355ee72a62b46bbab9360caad85df" :answer/id #uuid "caf49b0e-746b-56f6-bc08-dcf38b07a5a5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1+t\\sqrt{t}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-138902/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "638b5a0f-668d-502a-9c35-3845bd216efd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-138902/selection/dceb8599843d2455753fd3b610098e24c507c3f8042510eb7de7551e8d895488" :answer-field/choices ["q-138902/selection/dceb8599843d2455753fd3b610098e24c507c3f8042510eb7de7551e8d895488" "q-138902/selection/53e8c89f42976ed9e127d262e2f084ed51bc514efc5689e86b89aef2712cf66d" "q-138902/selection/2bd062a58e73398ad0d40efa61e4ff7757c19b4ffa3bc28d310e025ccf1dab75" "q-138902/selection/d8b0559a2ad692afd9d39c5b69c4476f36bad80b246506190982af18acbb4d61" "q-138902/selection/7340d7cc3561e241b79868dd2293b7678cb355ee72a62b46bbab9360caad85df"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-138902" :question/id #uuid "1d7a503f-e626-542c-b8d1-121fa51ecce9" :question/math-academy-id "q-138902" :question/problem "A body of mass $5\\,\\text{kg}$ is moving in a straight line along the $x$-axis under the action of a single force $F,$ measured in Newtons.\nAt time $t$ seconds, the position of the body is given by $s(t)=t-4\\sqrt{t}$ meters.\nFind the expression for the force acting on the body at time $t.$" :question/worked-solution "According to Newton’s second law\n\n$$\nF=ma,\n$$\n\n \nwhere $F$ is the force, $m$ is the mass, and $a$ is the acceleration.\n\nTo find the velocity $v(t),$ we differentiate the displacement $s(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}s}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t-4\\sqrt{t}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t-4{t}^{1/2}) \\\\  & =1-4\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\cdot {t}^{-1/2} \\\\  & =1-2{t}^{-1/2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the acceleration $a(t),$ we differentiate the velocity $v(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(1-2{t}^{-1/2}) \\\\  & =0-2\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{2})\\cdot {t}^{-3/2} \\\\  & ={t}^{-3/2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{t\\sqrt{t}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the force in Newtons is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F & =ma \\\\  & =5\\cdot (\\frac{1}{t\\sqrt{t}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{t\\sqrt{t}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-138902/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e955e35e-c45f-53b9-9f95-332d3e9c648f"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-138902"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-138769"] :question/problem "A body of mass $2\\,\\text{kg}$ is moving in a straight line along the $x$-axis under the action of a single force $F,$ measured in Newtons.\nAt time $t\\ge 0$ seconds, the velocity of the body is given by $v(t)=2{t}^{3}-3{t}^{2}-36t+2$ meters per second.\nCalculate the time at which the force acting on the body has zero magnitude." :question/worked-solution "According to Newton’s second law\n\n$$\nF=ma,\n$$\n\n \nwhere $F$ is the force, $m$ is the mass, and $a$ is the acceleration. \n\nTo find the acceleration $a(t),$ we differentiate the velocity $v(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2{t}^{3}-3{t}^{2}-36t+2) \\\\  & =6{t}^{2}-6t-36\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the mass is always positive, the force has zero magnitude when the acceleration equals zero. So, we set $a(t)=0$ and solve for $t:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6{t}^{2}-6t-36 & =0 \\\\ {t}^{2}-t-6 & =0 \\\\ (t-3)(t+2) & =0 \\\\ t & =-2,\\,3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $t\\ge 0,$ we disregard the negative solution. \n\nTherefore, the force has zero magnitude at $t=3\\,\\text{s}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-138916/selection/20b7bbf47e4159d425683ef96d3217c51e3972c1a9f75a41eff076cb46db14cf" :answer/id #uuid "8753c6f7-b969-5624-b5f3-e1ed6fb9fe62" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "t=8\\,\\text{s}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-138916/selection/8a8e4d981f70dfe4d9a30d5693836556ef8e6ad73d426cc0e557d2e2924ec9da" :answer/id #uuid "89e4bb85-0fe1-5c47-baf3-cf7ba0659cb1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "t=6\\,\\text{s}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-138916/selection/ba771dd41a37fcd1cabd147925488b8d4a7729bdbd79040a1a290ed8e3379a45" :answer/id #uuid "74fba03d-094d-555a-a4c4-d6c42e9a0dc3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "t=5\\,\\text{s}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-138916/selection/0ef8964ec0a97853c9de78640006c9267484858b6037a9251f0953a6b60d7cbd" :answer/id #uuid "48747f22-fc52-5e6b-9dbd-8b39acffbaa8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "t=3\\,\\text{s}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-138916/selection/d5def0cf746ec332768f9da3bbd3918000db01e741698aca0cf711527ac7cb72" :answer/id #uuid "175eaa1f-bf3e-5480-9ddb-18f8abe15e62" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "t=2\\,\\text{s}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-138916/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "9556cb54-d20c-5bb3-9707-5df22c1c108b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-138916/selection/ba771dd41a37fcd1cabd147925488b8d4a7729bdbd79040a1a290ed8e3379a45" :answer-field/choices ["q-138916/selection/20b7bbf47e4159d425683ef96d3217c51e3972c1a9f75a41eff076cb46db14cf" "q-138916/selection/8a8e4d981f70dfe4d9a30d5693836556ef8e6ad73d426cc0e557d2e2924ec9da" "q-138916/selection/ba771dd41a37fcd1cabd147925488b8d4a7729bdbd79040a1a290ed8e3379a45" "q-138916/selection/0ef8964ec0a97853c9de78640006c9267484858b6037a9251f0953a6b60d7cbd" "q-138916/selection/d5def0cf746ec332768f9da3bbd3918000db01e741698aca0cf711527ac7cb72"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-138916" :question/id #uuid "142d4d3c-01be-59e8-b6af-dd8e598fcc6e" :question/math-academy-id "q-138916" :question/problem "A body of mass $5\\,\\text{kg}$ is moving in a straight line along the $x$-axis under the action of a single force $F,$ measured in Newtons.\nAt time $t\\ge 0$ seconds, the position of the body is given by $s(t)={t}^{4}-150{t}^{2}+8$ meters.\nCalculate the time at which the force acting on the body has zero magnitude." :question/worked-solution "According to Newton’s second law\n\n$$\nF=ma,\n$$\n\n \nwhere $F$ is the force, $m$ is the mass, and $a$ is the acceleration. \n\nTo find the velocity $v(t),$ we differentiate the displacement $s(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}s}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{4}-150{t}^{2}+8) \\\\  & =4{t}^{3}-300t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the acceleration $a(t),$ we differentiate the velocity $v(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4{t}^{3}-300t) \\\\  & =12{t}^{2}-300\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the mass is always positive, the force has zero magnitude when the acceleration equals zero. So, we set $a(t)=0$ and solve for $t:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}12{t}^{2}-300 & =0 \\\\ 12{t}^{2} & =300 \\\\ {t}^{2} & =25 \\\\ t & =\\pm 5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $t\\ge 0,$ we disregard the negative solution. \n\nTherefore, the force has zero magnitude at $t=5\\,\\text{s}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-138916/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "266102e7-c8ef-55c9-8fcd-c3b6962f03b2"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-138916"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-138911/selection/1417faeeecb9abcec842b42bc312e82d299a8ac8f43684f3e20cdc301cbc99c4" :answer/id #uuid "26060830-13b8-5cdc-8158-83319a96fad0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "t=4\\,\\text{s}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-138911/selection/d5def0cf746ec332768f9da3bbd3918000db01e741698aca0cf711527ac7cb72" :answer/id #uuid "3cdaf7d2-2ebd-5e0d-9182-9f571241ec6e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "t=2\\,\\text{s}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-138911/selection/ba771dd41a37fcd1cabd147925488b8d4a7729bdbd79040a1a290ed8e3379a45" :answer/id #uuid "ce5b0859-2158-5130-9925-3bcb6cd2ad05" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "t=5\\,\\text{s}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-138911/selection/8a8e4d981f70dfe4d9a30d5693836556ef8e6ad73d426cc0e557d2e2924ec9da" :answer/id #uuid "0d08b910-cae3-5d0e-9f15-da49bda6e653" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "t=6\\,\\text{s}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-138911/selection/0ef8964ec0a97853c9de78640006c9267484858b6037a9251f0953a6b60d7cbd" :answer/id #uuid "f7f6738d-d214-53f2-affa-d863550c7c24" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "t=3\\,\\text{s}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-138911/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "cdea838b-e469-5954-b6b6-0b08d30a01b8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-138911/selection/1417faeeecb9abcec842b42bc312e82d299a8ac8f43684f3e20cdc301cbc99c4" :answer-field/choices ["q-138911/selection/1417faeeecb9abcec842b42bc312e82d299a8ac8f43684f3e20cdc301cbc99c4" "q-138911/selection/d5def0cf746ec332768f9da3bbd3918000db01e741698aca0cf711527ac7cb72" "q-138911/selection/ba771dd41a37fcd1cabd147925488b8d4a7729bdbd79040a1a290ed8e3379a45" "q-138911/selection/8a8e4d981f70dfe4d9a30d5693836556ef8e6ad73d426cc0e557d2e2924ec9da" "q-138911/selection/0ef8964ec0a97853c9de78640006c9267484858b6037a9251f0953a6b60d7cbd"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-138911" :question/id #uuid "163b7f1d-5e1e-53cc-9007-34ee797242e7" :question/math-academy-id "q-138911" :question/problem "A body of mass $5\\,\\text{kg}$ is moving in a straight line along the $x$-axis under the action of a single force $F,$ measured in Newtons.\nAt time $t\\ge 0$ seconds, the velocity of the body is given by $v(t)={t}^{3}-3{t}^{2}-24t+8$ meters per second.\nCalculate the time at which the force acting on the body has zero magnitude." :question/worked-solution "According to Newton’s second law\n\n$$\nF=ma,\n$$\n\n \nwhere $F$ is the force, $m$ is the mass, and $a$ is the acceleration. \n\nTo find the acceleration $a(t),$ we differentiate the velocity $v(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{3}-3{t}^{2}-24t+8) \\\\  & =3{t}^{2}-6t-24\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the mass is always positive, the force has zero magnitude when the acceleration equals zero. So, we set $a(t)=0$ and solve for $t:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{t}^{2}-6t-24 & =0 \\\\ {t}^{2}-2t-8 & =0 \\\\ (t+2)(t-4) & =0 \\\\ t & =-2,\\,4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $t\\ge 0,$ we disregard the negative solution. \n\nTherefore, the force has zero magnitude at $t=4\\,\\text{s}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-138911/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "266102e7-c8ef-55c9-8fcd-c3b6962f03b2"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-138911"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-138912/selection/d5def0cf746ec332768f9da3bbd3918000db01e741698aca0cf711527ac7cb72" :answer/id #uuid "5e64792e-49cb-52f3-a6c0-6404c989f508" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "t=2\\,\\text{s}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-138912/selection/f232b2e21fa38e5671736495c79c8df9c368a8623cbe81147c1e4f08daca2644" :answer/id #uuid "ee3ae733-a0ac-5904-8c33-530d472249f3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "t=10\\,\\text{s}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-138912/selection/0ef8964ec0a97853c9de78640006c9267484858b6037a9251f0953a6b60d7cbd" :answer/id #uuid "dabab117-8064-519b-a9d9-a84ccd69c222" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "t=3\\,\\text{s}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-138912/selection/20b7bbf47e4159d425683ef96d3217c51e3972c1a9f75a41eff076cb46db14cf" :answer/id #uuid "8cd5fc9a-309f-5bcd-b9fd-cfd56130e0ed" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "t=8\\,\\text{s}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-138912/selection/8a8e4d981f70dfe4d9a30d5693836556ef8e6ad73d426cc0e557d2e2924ec9da" :answer/id #uuid "b9f54d68-3b62-5d77-8c54-b3083ceacd08" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "t=6\\,\\text{s}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-138912/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "8da7164d-0e13-5785-a481-bdbb442ef57a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-138912/selection/d5def0cf746ec332768f9da3bbd3918000db01e741698aca0cf711527ac7cb72" :answer-field/choices ["q-138912/selection/d5def0cf746ec332768f9da3bbd3918000db01e741698aca0cf711527ac7cb72" "q-138912/selection/f232b2e21fa38e5671736495c79c8df9c368a8623cbe81147c1e4f08daca2644" "q-138912/selection/0ef8964ec0a97853c9de78640006c9267484858b6037a9251f0953a6b60d7cbd" "q-138912/selection/20b7bbf47e4159d425683ef96d3217c51e3972c1a9f75a41eff076cb46db14cf" "q-138912/selection/8a8e4d981f70dfe4d9a30d5693836556ef8e6ad73d426cc0e557d2e2924ec9da"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-138912" :question/id #uuid "0c703448-496c-5606-b90b-425604c02e8c" :question/math-academy-id "q-138912" :question/problem "A body of mass $2\\,\\text{kg}$ is moving in a straight line along the $x$-axis under the action of a single force $F,$ measured in Newtons.\nAt time $t\\ge 0$ seconds, the velocity of the body is given by $v(t)=6{t}^{3}-9{t}^{2}-36t+2$ meters per second.\nCalculate the time at which the force acting on the body has zero magnitude." :question/worked-solution "According to Newton’s second law\n\n$$\nF=ma,\n$$\n\n \nwhere $F$ is the force, $m$ is the mass, and $a$ is the acceleration. \n\nTo find the acceleration $a(t),$ we differentiate the velocity $v(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(6{t}^{3}-9{t}^{2}-36t+2) \\\\  & =18{t}^{2}-18t-36\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the mass is always positive, the force has zero magnitude when the acceleration equals zero. So, we set $a(t)=0$ and solve for $t:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}18{t}^{2}-18t-36 & =0 \\\\ {t}^{2}-t-2 & =0 \\\\ (t+1)(t-2) & =0 \\\\ t & =-1,\\,2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $t\\ge 0,$ we disregard the negative solution. \n\nTherefore, the force has zero magnitude at $t=2\\,\\text{s}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-138912/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "266102e7-c8ef-55c9-8fcd-c3b6962f03b2"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-138912"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-138770"] :question/problem "A body of mass $1.5\\,\\text{kg}$ is moving in a straight line along the $x$-axis under the action of a single force $F,$ measured in Newtons.\nAt time $t\\ge 0$ seconds, the position of the body is given by $s(t)=2{t}^{3}-12{t}^{2}+t-5$ meters per second.\nCalculate the time at which the force acting on the body has zero magnitude." :question/worked-solution "According to Newton’s second law\n\n$$\nF=ma,\n$$\n\n \nwhere $F$ is the force, $m$ is the mass, and $a$ is the acceleration. \n\nTo find the velocity $v(t),$ we differentiate the displacement $s(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}s}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2{t}^{3}-12{t}^{2}+t-5) \\\\  & =6{t}^{2}-24t+1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the acceleration $a(t),$ we differentiate the velocity $v(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(6{t}^{2}-24t+1) \\\\  & =12t-24\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the mass is always positive, the force has zero magnitude when the acceleration equals zero. So, we set $a(t)=0$ and solve for $t:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}12t-24 & =0 \\\\ 12 & =24 \\\\ t & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the force has zero magnitude at $t=2\\,\\text{s}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-9454"] :question/problem "A body of mass $3 \\, \\textrm{kg}$ is moving in a straight line along the $x$-axis under the action of a single force $F,$ measured in Newtons $(\\textrm{N}).$\nAt time $t$ seconds, the velocity of the body is given by $v(t) =t^2- e^{t-4}$ meters per second.\nCalculate the magnitude of the force at time $t=4$ seconds." :question/worked-solution "According to Newton’s second law\n\n$$\nF=ma,\n$$\n\n \nwhere $F$ is the force, $m$ is the mass, and $a$ is the acceleration.\n\nTo find the acceleration $a(t),$ we differentiate the velocity $v(t){:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2}-{e}^{t-4}) \\\\  & =2t-{e}^{t-4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs a result, the acceleration at $t=4 \\, \\textrm{s}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a & =2(4)-{e}^{4-4} \\\\  & =8-1 \\\\  & =7\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the force, in Newtons, is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F & =ma \\\\  & =3\\cdot (7) \\\\  & =21.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the magnitude of the force is\n\n$$\n|F| = |21| = 21 \\, \\textrm{N}.\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-9859"] :question/problem "A body of mass $2 \\, \\textrm{kg}$ is moving in a straight line along the $x$-axis under the action of a single force $F,$ measured in Newtons.\nAt time $t$ seconds, the position of the body is given by $s(t) = e^{3t-6} + t^2$ meters. Find the expression for the force acting on the body at time $t.$" :question/worked-solution "According to Newton’s second law\n\n$$\nF=ma,\n$$\n\n \nwhere $F$ is the force, $m$ is the mass, and $a$ is the acceleration.\n\nTo find the velocity $v(t),$ we differentiate the displacement $s(t){:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}s}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{3t-6}+{t}^{2}) \\\\  & =3{e}^{3t-6}+2t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the acceleration $a(t),$ we differentiate the velocity $v(t){:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3{e}^{3t-6}+2t) \\\\  & =9{e}^{3t-6}+2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the force acting on the body, in Newtons, is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F & =ma \\\\  & =2\\cdot (9{e}^{3t-6}+2) \\\\  & =18{e}^{3t-6}+4.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-9860"] :question/problem "A body of mass $2 \\, \\textrm{kg}$ moves in a straight line along the $x$-axis under the action of a single force $F,$ measured in Newtons.\nAt time $t\\geq 0$ seconds, the velocity of the body is given by $v(t) =2t^3-12t^2-30t+5$ meters per second.\nCalculate the time when the force acting on the body has a magnitude of zero." :question/worked-solution "According to Newton’s second law\n\n$$\nF=ma,\n$$\n\n \nwhere $F$ is the force, $m$ is the mass, and $a$ is the acceleration. \n\nTo find the acceleration $a(t),$ we differentiate the velocity $v(t){:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2{t}^{3}-12{t}^{2}-30t+5) \\\\  & =6{t}^{2}-24t-30\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the mass is always positive, the force has zero magnitude when the acceleration equals zero. So, we set $a(t)=0$ and solve for $t{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6{t}^{2}-24t-30 & =0 \\\\ {t}^{2}-4t-5 & =0 \\\\ (t+1)(t-5) & =0 \\\\ t & =-1,\\,5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $t \\geq 0,$ we disregard the negative solution. \n\nTherefore, the force has zero magnitude when $t=5 \\, \\textrm{s}.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
